\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{A raw root presentation, a Reedy-fibrant presentation, and a categorical localization are distinct objects. Neither horizontal composites nor symmetry are primitive. Their existence or encoding is supplied by additional constructions.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Reedy fibrancy controls mapping and restriction fibrations; it does not identify all diagrams that should be categorically equivalent.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Using one unnamed notion of fibrancy or equivalence for all three roles.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0004}, \ref{at-fd-0005}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional until the comparisons are formalized.}
}
